 "batch_notes": "1) KNOWN FAILURE labelling is inconsistent with the rubric's pin definition: geo (pbt_convex_hull_contains_all_input_points, pbt_convex_hull_no_panic_on_any_finite_coords, pbt_simplify_matches_simplify_idx) and fjall (insert_within_documented_key_limit_does_not_panic) say KNOWN FAILURE on the unrestricted general property that found the bug, while siblings are restricted to keep passing; I tagged pin only where the body was narrowed or boosted toward the failure (fixed known_failure_*, fancy-regex known_failure, geohash lat90 and decode_never_panics, gif KNOWN_FAILURE). The bug-rate-without-pins figure will differ depending on whether the report follows the doc marker or the body shape. 2) std BTreeMap/BTreeSet used as a container model (fjall, fst) is classified model-oracle, not external-oracle, even though the rubric lists stdlib under external; the rubric could say explicitly which it wants for a std container standing in as the model. 3) Rubric gap: 'expected value derived from the library's own output on a simpler spec' (format_num layout/fill/zero-padded-grouping/integer-rounding, geohash neighbour) sits between internal-consistency, model-oracle and spec-postcondition; I split by whether a substantive test-side computation (pad()) produced the expectation. 4) Resource/allocation properties (gif memory limit on the pixel path and skip path, fancy-regex backtrack limit) do not fit any category well; tagged interesting. 5) fixed: most properties are macro invocations with no doc comment, so several classifications rest on the name plus the visible sibling (medium confidence on parse_variants_agree, neg/abs). 6) format_num is a differential study with an unusual oracle (python3 child process) and one hybrid oracle (Python digits + test-side d3 SI model). 7) Bug records with empty test fields (evalexpr/5, full_moon/2) were not produced by the batch's properties; full_moon/2 bundles two distinct issues, only one of which a property gated around. 8) geohash/2 is status fixed upstream but still carried; geo bug records name general properties directly, so those three bugs count as found by unrestricted properties."
